MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The early Rolling Stones feel like a natural next choice because their blues-driven guitar connects with my recent interest in Hendrix and Clapton.",
    "Second Hand Heart appeals because its guitar-driven country connects with Blown Away, while the Eagles also fit the country-rock side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Earth Wind & Fire's funk and dance-oriented soul and The Endless River's atmospheric instrumentals miss my current interest in rootsy vocals and guitar-led songs.",
    "25 feels less connected to my recent blues and roots-rock listening, and I cannot judge whether the two collections with unidentified artists connect to it at all."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Familiar older acts seem to count too heavily; sharing an era does not make atmospheric rock or dance-oriented soul fit my current mood.",
    "The repeated greatest-hits collections assume I want career overviews, even though my recent choices have been individual albums."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection that matters most right now is blues-influenced guitar and rootsy singing, with room for guitar-driven country.",
    "An appealing style alone is not enough for me to choose something this visit: the Eagles, Sound & Color, and the Mamas & the Papas interest me, but the Stones and Second Hand Heart give me stronger reasons to act."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my blues and country interests but stretch them too broadly into familiar acts and hits collections."
}
